=product @PRODUCER@ @BASE@ MAVEN @PCSIVERSION@ full
1 'PRODUCER
=prompt @PRODUCER@
1 'PRODUCT
=prompt Apache Maven @VERSION@ for OpenVMS
1 'NOTICE
=prompt Apache Maven is under the Apache License 2.0; see [MAVEN]LICENSE.
1 RELEASE_NOTES
=prompt Documentation is in [MAVEN]README.VMS under the installation directory.
1 POST_INSTALL
=prompt Post-installation tasks for Apache Maven
    At system startup: to define MAVEN$ROOT at every boot, add this line to
    SYS$MANAGER:SYSTARTUP_VMS.COM:
    $ @SYS$STARTUP:MAVEN$STARTUP.COM
    For each user: to define the MVN command, add this line to LOGIN.COM:
    $ @MAVEN$ROOT:[000000]MAVEN$SETUP.COM
    Maven needs VSI OpenJDK 8 (SYS$STARTUP:OPENJDK$SETUP.COM).

PRODUCT REMOVE MAVEN removes the product and deassigns MAVEN$ROOT.
